.env.local*

# Env patterns stay ignored, but the committed template must stay trackable
# even if a tool adds a broad `.env*` rule (the Vercel CLI does this on
# `vercel link`), which would otherwise hide it. AGENTS.md requires a 1:1
# list of every env var in .env.example. `git add -f` would also work, but
# the explicit negation survives the next tool that rewrites this file.
!.env.example

# vitest JSON reporter output (rtk/vitest artifact)
.vitest/
